sentences.text:
1 "i)-issue a writ order or direction in the nature of Certiorari or likewise thereby quashing the Notification dated 03.05.2023 (Annexure No. 1) issued under Section 3D(2), The National Highway Act, 1956 by the Ministry of Road Transport and Highways, Government of India;
(ii)-issue a writ, order or direction in the nature of Certiorari or likewise thereby quashing the arbitrary and unjust decision/action/object of the respondents to deviate from the existing Kanpur-Lucknow highway/road in the matter of construction of elevated road under the Kanpur- Lucknow Expressway/National Expressway-6 (NE-6) at Banthra, Lucknow for which purpose additional land of the petitioners is sought to be acquired, after summoning the same;
(iii)-issue a writ, order or direction in the nature of Mandamus or likewise thereby commanding the opposite parties competent not to deviate from the median of the existing Kanpur-Lucknow highway/road in the matter of construction of elevated road under the Kanpur-Lucknow Expressway/National Expressway-6 (NE-6) at Banthra, Lucknow for which purpose additional land of the petitioners is sought to be acquired.
(iv)-issue a writ, order or direction in the nature of Mandamus or likewise thereby commanding the State of U.P., respondent no. 3, to consider restricting the speed of motor vehicles in the interest of public safety and convenience, as against the maximum speed limit laid down for the National Highways and Expressways in the State by exercising powers conferred under Sub-section (2) of Section 112, The Motor Vehicle Act, 1988 keeping in view the grim scenario as to the soaring of road accidents in the State of U.P."
3.
